Lamb Shanks with Mustard and Mint
Serves: 4
Prep: 15 min
Cook: 2 hr
Total: 2¼ hr
Equipment: Dutch oven or braiser, Tongs, Ladle

Serve: Ladle sauce over the shanks and scatter with mint.
  Reduce (heat): Shanks to a platter. Simmer sauce on the hob to about **{360 ml}** (1½ cups). Skim the fat. Season.
    Braise (heat, 2–2½ hr): Add stock, Worcestershire and mustard; scrape the pan. Lay mint on top, cover, into the oven until meat **falls off the bone**.
      Deglaze (heat, ~1 min): Stir in shallots and garlic for **15 s**, then add wine at once. Boil **1 min**.
        Sear (heat, ~8 min): Oven to **180 °C / 350 °F**. Oil **smoking** in the pot. Season shanks; brown on all sides.
          - 2 Tbsp | Olive oil
          - 4 | Lamb shanks | about 1.4 kg · 3 lb
          - to taste | Kosher salt & pepper
        Mince: Peel and finely mince both, about **{3 Tbsp}** shallot and **{4 tsp}** garlic.
          - 2 | Shallots
          - 4 cloves | Garlic
        - 240 ml = 1 cup | Dry white wine
      - 480 ml = 2 cups | Chicken or beef stock | low-sodium
      - 2 Tbsp | Worcestershire sauce
      - 2 Tbsp | Wholegrain mustard
      - ½ bunch | Fresh mint | left on the stem
    - to taste | Salt & pepper
  Chop (then set aside): Pick the leaves and chop roughly.
    - ½ bunch | Fresh mint
